{"v":1,"db":{"url":"https://davan-lessonplan-archive-default-rtdb.asia-southeast1.firebasedatabase.app","key":"AIzaSyDBfwaUiCP_5tLPgCV2yZSeeWRnwnvnkDQ","root":"learn"},"pass":0.8,"tracks":[{"id":"quant","g":"apt","name":"Quant","emoji":"🧮","levels":[{"n":1,"name":"Percentages","tag":"TCS NQT pattern","cards":[{"t":"What is %","b":"Per cent means 'out of 100'. 25% = 25/100 = 1/4.","box":"x% of N = N × x ÷ 100","kn":"ಶೇಕಡಾ = 100 ರಲ್ಲಿ ಎಷ್ಟು ಭಾಗ."},{"t":"5-second fractions","b":"Learn these and skip long division.","box":"50% = 1/2 · 25% = 1/4 · 20% = 1/5 · 12.5% = 1/8 · 10% = 1/10","kn":"ಈ ಭಿನ್ನರಾಶಿಗಳನ್ನು ನೆನಪಿಡಿ, ಲೆಕ್ಕ ಬೇಗ ಆಗುತ್ತದೆ."},{"t":"Up and down","b":"A 20% rise means × 1.2. A 10% fall means × 0.9.","box":"New = Old × (100 ± x) ÷ 100","kn":"ಹೆಚ್ಚಳ ×1.2, ಇಳಿಕೆ ×0.9"}],"qs":[{"q":"20% of 450 = ?","o":["80","90","95","100"],"a":1,"e":"20% = 1/5, so 450 ÷ 5 = 90.","id":"quant1_1"},{"q":"What % of 80 is 20?","o":["20%","25%","30%","40%"],"a":1,"e":"20/80 = 1/4 = 25%.","id":"quant1_2"},{"q":"Your first salary is ₹25,000. You get a 12% hike. New salary?","o":["₹27,000","₹28,000","₹28,500","₹30,000"],"a":1,"e":"25,000 × 1.12 = 28,000.","tag":"Workplace situation","id":"quant1_3"},{"q":"A phone costs ₹12,000 with a 10% discount. You pay?","o":["₹10,800","₹11,000","₹10,000","₹11,200"],"a":0,"e":"12,000 × 0.9 = 10,800.","id":"quant1_4"},{"q":"A town of 5,000 grows 10% a year. After 2 years?","o":["6,000","6,050","6,100","5,500"],"a":1,"e":"5,000 × 1.1 = 5,500 → × 1.1 = 6,050.","id":"quant1_5"},{"q":"60 is 40% of what number?","o":["120","140","150","160"],"a":2,"e":"60 ÷ 0.4 = 150.","id":"quant1_6"},{"q":"Petrol price goes up 25%. By what % must you cut use to spend the same?","o":["20%","25%","15%","30%"],"a":0,"e":"Rise 1/4 → cut 1/(4+1) = 1/5 = 20%.","id":"quant1_7"},{"q":"You score 360 out of 450. Your percentage?","o":["75%","80%","85%","90%"],"a":1,"e":"360/450 = 0.8 = 80%.","id":"quant1_8"}]},{"n":2,"name":"Profit & loss","tag":"TCS NQT + AMCAT pattern","cards":[{"t":"CP and SP","b":"CP = what the shop paid. SP = what you pay the shop.","box":"Profit = SP − CP · Loss = CP − SP","kn":"CP ಕೊಂಡ ಬೆಲೆ, SP ಮಾರಿದ ಬೆಲೆ."},{"t":"% is always on COST","b":"Divide the profit by the cost price, never by the selling price.","box":"Profit % = Profit ÷ CP × 100","kn":"ಲಾಭವನ್ನು ಕೊಂಡ ಬೆಲೆಯಿಂದ ಭಾಗಿಸಿ."},{"t":"Find SP fast","b":"20% profit means SP = 120% of CP. 10% loss means SP = 90% of CP.","box":"SP = CP × (100 + P%) ÷ 100","kn":"ಲಾಭ 20% → SP = CP × 1.2"}],"qs":[{"q":"Your shop buys a phone cover for ₹400 and sells it for ₹500. Profit %?","o":["20%","25%","15%","30%"],"a":1,"e":"Profit 100 ÷ CP 400 = 1/4 = 25%.","tag":"Workplace situation","id":"quant2_1"},{"q":"CP ₹250, SP ₹200. Loss %?","o":["20%","25%","50%","15%"],"a":0,"e":"Loss 50 ÷ 250 = 20%.","id":"quant2_2"},{"q":"CP ₹600, profit 15%. SP?","o":["₹660","₹690","₹700","₹720"],"a":1,"e":"600 × 1.15 = 690.","id":"quant2_3"},{"q":"Sold at ₹1,200 with 20% profit. CP?","o":["₹960","₹1,000","₹1,040","₹1,100"],"a":1,"e":"1,200 ÷ 1.2 = 1,000.","id":"quant2_4"},{"q":"Goods marked 40% above cost, then 10% discount. Profit %?","o":["30%","26%","36%","24%"],"a":1,"e":"1.4 × 0.9 = 1.26 → 26%.","id":"quant2_5"},{"q":"You buy 10 pens for ₹100 and sell each for ₹12. Profit %?","o":["12%","20%","2%","25%"],"a":1,"e":"Sell 120, cost 100 → 20%.","id":"quant2_6"},{"q":"SP of 12 items = CP of 15 items. Profit %?","o":["20%","25%","30%","15%"],"a":1,"e":"Take CP of 1 item = 1: cost 12, sell 15 → 3/12 = 25%.","id":"quant2_7"},{"q":"CP ₹800, sold at 5% loss. SP?","o":["₹740","₹760","₹780","₹790"],"a":1,"e":"800 × 0.95 = 760.","id":"quant2_8"}]}]},{"id":"reason","g":"apt","name":"Reasoning","emoji":"🧩","levels":[{"n":1,"name":"Number & letter series","tag":"AMCAT pattern","cards":[{"t":"Look at the gaps","b":"Write the difference between each pair. The pattern is usually in the gaps.","box":"2, 6, 12, 20 → gaps +4, +6, +8","kn":"ಎರಡು ಸಂಖ್ಯೆಗಳ ನಡುವಿನ ವ್ಯತ್ಯಾಸ ನೋಡಿ."},{"t":"× and ÷ series","b":"If the gaps grow fast, try multiplying.","box":"3, 9, 27 → × 3 each time","kn":"ವೇಗವಾಗಿ ಬೆಳೆದರೆ ಗುಣಾಕಾರ ಇರಬಹುದು."},{"t":"Letters are numbers","b":"A = 1, B = 2 … Z = 26. Count jumps between letters.","box":"A, C, E → +2 each","kn":"ಅಕ್ಷರಗಳಿಗೆ ಸಂಖ್ಯೆ ಕೊಡಿ: A=1, B=2"}],"qs":[{"q":"2, 6, 12, 20, 30, ?","o":["36","40","42","44"],"a":2,"e":"Gaps +4 +6 +8 +10 → next +12 → 42.","id":"reason1_1"},{"q":"3, 9, 27, 81, ?","o":["162","243","216","324"],"a":1,"e":"× 3 each time → 243.","id":"reason1_2"},{"q":"1, 4, 9, 16, 25, ?","o":["30","35","36","49"],"a":2,"e":"Squares: 6 × 6 = 36.","id":"reason1_3"},{"q":"A, C, E, G, ?","o":["H","I","J","K"],"a":1,"e":"+2 letters each time → I.","id":"reason1_4"},{"q":"5, 10, 20, 40, ?","o":["60","70","80","90"],"a":2,"e":"× 2 → 80.","id":"reason1_5"},{"q":"Z, X, V, T, ?","o":["S","R","Q","P"],"a":1,"e":"−2 letters each time → R.","id":"reason1_6"},{"q":"7, 14, 28, 56, ?","o":["84","98","112","120"],"a":2,"e":"× 2 → 112.","id":"reason1_7"},{"q":"2, 3, 5, 8, 12, ?","o":["15","16","17","18"],"a":2,"e":"Gaps +1 +2 +3 +4 → next +5 → 17.","id":"reason1_8"}]},{"n":2,"name":"Coding-decoding","tag":"Infosys pattern","cards":[{"t":"Shift the letters","b":"Most codes move every letter forward or back by the same number.","box":"CAT → DBU (each +1)","kn":"ಪ್ರತಿ ಅಕ್ಷರ ಒಂದೇ ಸಂಖ್ಯೆ ಮುಂದೆ/ಹಿಂದೆ."},{"t":"Reverse codes","b":"Some codes just write the word backwards.","box":"ROSE → ESOR","kn":"ಪದವನ್ನು ಹಿಂದಿನಿಂದ ಬರೆಯುವುದು."},{"t":"Number codes","b":"Letters can become their place numbers (A=1) or reverse places (A=26).","box":"BAD = 2 + 1 + 4 = 7","kn":"A=1 ಅಥವಾ A=26 ಎರಡೂ ಸಾಧ್ಯ."}],"qs":[{"q":"CAT → DBU. DOG → ?","o":["EPH","EPI","FPH","DPH"],"a":0,"e":"Each letter +1: D→E, O→P, G→H.","id":"reason2_1"},{"q":"If A = 1, B = 2 … then BAD = ?","o":["7","8","6","9"],"a":0,"e":"2 + 1 + 4 = 7.","id":"reason2_2"},{"q":"ROSE → ESOR. LIME → ?","o":["EMIL","ELIM","MILE","EMLI"],"a":0,"e":"Written backwards.","id":"reason2_3"},{"q":"BOOK → CPPL. PEN → ?","o":["QFO","QFN","PFO","QEO"],"a":0,"e":"Each letter +1.","id":"reason2_4"},{"q":"FISH → GJTI. The code moves each letter by?","o":["+1","+2","−1","0"],"a":0,"e":"F→G, I→J: +1.","id":"reason2_5"},{"q":"If A = 26, B = 25 … then C = ?","o":["24","23","3","25"],"a":0,"e":"Reverse order: C = 24.","id":"reason2_6"},{"q":"P = 1, A = 2, E = 3, R = 5. REAP = ?","o":["5321","5231","5312","3521"],"a":0,"e":"R5 E3 A2 P1.","id":"reason2_7"},{"q":"MANGO → NBOHP. APPLE → ?","o":["BQQMF","BQQME","AQQMF","BPPMF"],"a":0,"e":"Each letter +1.","id":"reason2_8"}]}]},{"id":"verbal","g":"apt","name":"Verbal","emoji":"📖","levels":[{"n":1,"name":"Errors & articles","tag":"Wipro pattern","cards":[{"t":"a or an?","b":"Go by the SOUND, not the letter.","box":"an honest man · a university · an MBA","kn":"ಶಬ್ದ ಸ್ವರದಿಂದ ಶುರುವಾದರೆ 'an'."},{"t":"the","b":"Use 'the' for one special thing everyone knows.","box":"the sun · the Principal of Davan","kn":"ಒಂದೇ ಇರುವ ವಸ್ತುವಿಗೆ 'the'."},{"t":"Common mistakes","b":"Do not use -ing with have, know, like.","box":"I have two brothers (not 'am having')","kn":"'I am having' ಬದಲು 'I have'."}],"qs":[{"q":"He is ___ honest man.","o":["a","an","the","no article"],"a":1,"e":"'Honest' starts with an 'o' sound → an.","id":"verbal1_1"},{"q":"I ___ two brothers.","o":["am having","have","having","has"],"a":1,"e":"'Have' (possession) has no -ing.","id":"verbal1_2"},{"q":"She ___ to college every day.","o":["go","goes","going","gone"],"a":1,"e":"She + present simple → goes.","id":"verbal1_3"},{"q":"___ sun rises in the east.","o":["A","An","The","No article"],"a":2,"e":"Only one sun → the.","id":"verbal1_4"},{"q":"Find the error: 'Each of the students have a book.'","o":["Each of","the students","have","a book"],"a":2,"e":"'Each' is singular → has.","id":"verbal1_5"},{"q":"I am waiting ___ the bus.","o":["to","for","on","at"],"a":1,"e":"wait for.","id":"verbal1_6"},{"q":"She is good ___ maths.","o":["in","at","on","with"],"a":1,"e":"good at.","id":"verbal1_7"},{"q":"Neither he nor I ___ ready.","o":["am","is","are","be"],"a":0,"e":"The verb follows the nearer subject 'I' → am.","id":"verbal1_8"}]},{"n":2,"name":"Synonyms & fill-ups","tag":"Accenture pattern","cards":[{"t":"Synonym","b":"A word with the SAME meaning.","box":"Reliable = Dependable","kn":"ಒಂದೇ ಅರ್ಥದ ಪದ."},{"t":"Antonym","b":"A word with the OPPOSITE meaning.","box":"Accept ↔ Reject","kn":"ವಿರುದ್ಧ ಅರ್ಥದ ಪದ."},{"t":"Fill the blank","b":"Read the whole sentence first, then check the word form (verb / noun).","box":"Please ___ the form → submit (verb)","kn":"ಪೂರ್ಣ ವಾಕ್ಯ ಓದಿ ನಂತರ ಉತ್ತರಿಸಿ."}],"qs":[{"q":"Synonym of 'Punctual'","o":["On time","Lazy","Loud","Rich"],"a":0,"e":"Punctual = always on time.","id":"verbal2_1"},{"q":"Antonym of 'Expand'","o":["Grow","Shrink","Open","Spread"],"a":1,"e":"Expand ↔ shrink.","id":"verbal2_2"},{"q":"Synonym of 'Diligent'","o":["Hard-working","Careless","Angry","Quiet"],"a":0,"e":"Diligent = hard-working.","id":"verbal2_3"},{"q":"Antonym of 'Ancient'","o":["Old","Modern","Big","Famous"],"a":1,"e":"Ancient ↔ modern.","id":"verbal2_4"},{"q":"The manager ___ my leave.","o":["approved","approve","approval","approving"],"a":0,"e":"Past tense verb → approved.","id":"verbal2_5"},{"q":"Synonym of 'Reliable'","o":["Dependable","Weak","Funny","Rude"],"a":0,"e":"Reliable = dependable.","id":"verbal2_6"},{"q":"Antonym of 'Accept'","o":["Take","Reject","Agree","Allow"],"a":1,"e":"Accept ↔ reject.","id":"verbal2_7"},{"q":"Please ___ the form before 5 pm.","o":["submit","submission","submitted","submitting"],"a":0,"e":"After 'please' → base verb.","id":"verbal2_8"}]}]},{"id":"english","g":"eng","name":"English","emoji":"🗣️","levels":[{"n":1,"name":"Self-introduction & HR","tag":"HR interview","cards":[{"t":"Tell me about yourself","b":"Answer in 60 seconds.","box":"Name → course → 1 project → 1 strength → why this company","kn":"ಹೆಸರು → ಕೋರ್ಸ್ → ಪ್ರಾಜೆಕ್ಟ್ → ಶಕ್ತಿ → ಏಕೆ ಈ ಕಂಪನಿ"},{"t":"Polite phrases","b":"Start requests with 'Could you please' or 'May I'.","box":"Could you please share the details?","kn":"ವಿನಯದಿಂದ ಕೇಳಿ: Could you please…"},{"t":"Say 'I am', not 'Myself'","b":"'Myself Ananya' is a common Indian-English mistake.","box":"I am Ananya. / My name is Ananya.","kn":"'Myself …' ಬದಲು 'I am …'"}],"qs":[{"q":"Best start for 'Tell me about yourself'","o":["My name is Ananya. I am a final-year BCA student…","I was born in 2004 in a hospital…","My father's name is…","I like movies and songs…"],"a":0,"e":"Start with who you are now and your course.","id":"english1_1"},{"q":"Polite way to ask","o":["Give me the details.","Could you please share the details?","Tell details now.","Details?"],"a":1,"e":"'Could you please…' is polite.","id":"english1_2"},{"q":"Correct sentence","o":["I am having 2 years experience.","I have 2 years of experience.","I have experience of 2 year.","I am 2 years experience."],"a":1,"e":"have + years of experience.","id":"english1_3"},{"q":"Best answer to 'What is your weakness?'","o":["I have no weakness.","I take long on details, so now I set time limits.","I am lazy.","I don't know."],"a":1,"e":"Name a real weakness and how you fix it.","id":"english1_4"},{"q":"Greeting in an email to HR you don't know","o":["Hi buddy,","Dear Sir/Madam,","Hey,","Yo,"],"a":1,"e":"Formal: Dear Sir/Madam.","id":"english1_5"},{"q":"'Thank you for the opportunity' means","o":["I am grateful for the chance","I am angry","I want money","I am leaving"],"a":0,"e":"Opportunity = chance.","id":"english1_6"},{"q":"Correct way to introduce yourself","o":["Myself Ananya.","I am Ananya.","Me Ananya.","Ananya myself."],"a":1,"e":"'I am …'","id":"english1_7"},{"q":"Best way to end an interview","o":["Bye.","Thank you for your time. I look forward to hearing from you.","OK, done.","See you."],"a":1,"e":"Thank them and show interest.","id":"english1_8"}]},{"n":2,"name":"Office emails & calls","tag":"Workplace situation","cards":[{"t":"Clear subject line","b":"Say what and when.","box":"Leave request for 20 Oct (fever)","kn":"ವಿಷಯ ಸ್ಪಷ್ಟವಾಗಿರಲಿ."},{"t":"Phone manners","b":"Greet, say the place and your name, offer help.","box":"Good morning, Davan Accounts, Ananya speaking.","kn":"ಶುಭಾಶಯ + ಹೆಸರು + ಸಹಾಯ."},{"t":"Avoid old phrases","b":"'Revert back' and 'do the needful' are unclear.","box":"I will reply by 5 pm today.","kn":"ಸ್ಪಷ್ಟವಾಗಿ ಬರೆಯಿರಿ."}],"qs":[{"q":"Best subject line for leave","o":["Leave","Leave request for 20 Oct (fever)","Hi","Urgent!!!"],"a":1,"e":"Says what and when.","id":"english2_1"},{"q":"Answering an office phone","o":["Hello, who is this?","Good morning, Davan Accounts, Ananya speaking. How may I help you?","Yes?","Tell."],"a":1,"e":"Greet + place + name + help.","id":"english2_2"},{"q":"'Please find attached' means","o":["the file is with this email","call me","I am busy","delete it"],"a":0,"e":"There is an attachment.","id":"english2_3"},{"q":"Correct","o":["I will revert back.","I will reply soon.","I will revert you back.","I revert."],"a":1,"e":"Simple and clear.","id":"english2_4"},{"q":"Asking someone to repeat","o":["What?","Sorry, could you repeat that, please?","Again.","Huh?"],"a":1,"e":"Polite request.","id":"english2_5"},{"q":"Clearest request","o":["Kindly do the needful.","Please send the report by 5 pm today.","Do needful.","Send."],"a":1,"e":"Says what and by when.","id":"english2_6"},{"q":"Best email closing","o":["Regards, Ananya K","Bye bye","OK tata","From me"],"a":0,"e":"Regards + full name.","id":"english2_7"},{"q":"Correct","o":["I'm running late, I'll be there by 10:15.","I'm late running.","Running late I'm.","Late I running."],"a":0,"e":"Natural English.","id":"english2_8"}]}]},{"id":"bca","g":"tech","course":"BCA","name":"BCA Technical","emoji":"💻","levels":[{"n":1,"name":"C basics","tag":"Infosys pattern","cards":[{"t":"Integer maths","b":"In C, int / int drops the decimal.","box":"7 / 2 = 3 · 7 % 2 = 1","kn":"int / int → ದಶಮಾಂಶ ಹೋಗುತ್ತದೆ."},{"t":"Loops","b":"do-while runs at least once; for and while may run zero times.","box":"do { … } while (x);","kn":"do-while ಕನಿಷ್ಠ ಒಮ್ಮೆ ನಡೆಯುತ್ತದೆ."},{"t":"Arrays & scanf","b":"Arrays start at index 0. scanf needs the address (&).","box":"scanf(\"%d\", &n);","kn":"ಅರೇ 0 ಇಂದ ಶುರು."}],"qs":[{"q":"int x = 5; x += 3; printf(\"%d\", x * 2);","o":["16","13","10","Error"],"a":0,"e":"x becomes 8, 8 × 2 = 16.","id":"bca1_1"},{"q":"printf(\"%d\", 7 / 2);","o":["3.5","3","4","Error"],"a":1,"e":"Integer division → 3.","id":"bca1_2"},{"q":"printf(\"%d\", 7 % 3);","o":["1","2","0","3"],"a":0,"e":"Remainder of 7 ÷ 3 = 1.","id":"bca1_3"},{"q":"Size of char in C (bytes)","o":["1","2","4","8"],"a":0,"e":"char is 1 byte.","id":"bca1_4"},{"q":"Which loop always runs at least once?","o":["for","while","do-while","none"],"a":2,"e":"Condition is checked at the end.","id":"bca1_5"},{"q":"int a = 10; if (a > 5) a = a - 5; printf(\"%d\", a);","o":["10","5","0","15"],"a":1,"e":"10 > 5 → a = 5.","id":"bca1_6"},{"q":"Array index in C starts at","o":["0","1","-1","any number"],"a":0,"e":"First element is a[0].","id":"bca1_7"},{"q":"Correct way to read an int","o":["scanf(\"%d\", &n);","scanf(\"%d\", n);","scan(\"%d\", &n);","read(n);"],"a":0,"e":"scanf needs &n.","id":"bca1_8"}]},{"n":2,"name":"DBMS & SQL","tag":"TCS NQT pattern","cards":[{"t":"SELECT","b":"SELECT reads rows; WHERE filters rows; ORDER BY sorts.","box":"SELECT name FROM students WHERE marks > 60 ORDER BY marks DESC;","kn":"SELECT ಓದಲು, WHERE ಆರಿಸಲು."},{"t":"Keys","b":"Primary key: unique and never NULL. One per table.","box":"PRIMARY KEY (urn)","kn":"ಪ್ರೈಮರಿ ಕೀ NULL ಆಗುವುದಿಲ್ಲ."},{"t":"GROUP BY + HAVING","b":"WHERE filters rows before grouping, HAVING filters groups after.","box":"GROUP BY class HAVING COUNT(*) > 30","kn":"HAVING ಗುಂಪುಗಳ ನಂತರ."}],"qs":[{"q":"Command to read data","o":["SELECT","GET","OPEN","SHOW"],"a":0,"e":"SELECT reads rows.","id":"bca2_1"},{"q":"Can a primary key be NULL?","o":["Yes","No","Only once","Only in MySQL"],"a":1,"e":"Never NULL.","id":"bca2_2"},{"q":"Remove all rows but keep the table","o":["DELETE TABLE","DROP","TRUNCATE","REMOVE"],"a":2,"e":"TRUNCATE empties it; DROP deletes the table.","id":"bca2_3"},{"q":"Filter groups after GROUP BY","o":["WHERE","HAVING","ORDER BY","FILTER"],"a":1,"e":"HAVING works on groups.","id":"bca2_4"},{"q":"COUNT(*) counts","o":["all rows","only non-NULL values","columns","tables"],"a":0,"e":"COUNT(*) counts every row.","id":"bca2_5"},{"q":"Sort from high to low","o":["ORDER BY x DESC","SORT x DOWN","ORDER x DESC","GROUP BY x DESC"],"a":0,"e":"ORDER BY … DESC.","id":"bca2_6"},{"q":"Join that keeps only rows matching in both tables","o":["INNER JOIN","LEFT JOIN","FULL JOIN","CROSS JOIN"],"a":0,"e":"INNER JOIN.","id":"bca2_7"},{"q":"Normalisation mainly reduces","o":["Duplicate data","Speed","Security","Tables"],"a":0,"e":"It removes redundancy.","id":"bca2_8"}]}]},{"id":"bba","g":"tech","course":"BBA","name":"BBA Technical","emoji":"📊","levels":[{"n":1,"name":"Management & marketing","tag":"HR / technical interview","cards":[{"t":"Functions of management","b":"Planning, organising, directing and controlling.","box":"P-O-D-C","kn":"ಯೋಜನೆ, ಸಂಘಟನೆ, ನಿರ್ದೇಶನ, ನಿಯಂತ್ರಣ"},{"t":"SWOT","b":"Strengths, Weaknesses (inside) · Opportunities, Threats (outside).","box":"S W O T","kn":"ಒಳಗಿನ ಶಕ್ತಿ/ದೌರ್ಬಲ್ಯ, ಹೊರಗಿನ ಅವಕಾಶ/ಅಪಾಯ"},{"t":"4 Ps","b":"Product, Price, Place, Promotion.","box":"What · how much · where · how people hear","kn":"ಉತ್ಪನ್ನ, ಬೆಲೆ, ಸ್ಥಳ, ಪ್ರಚಾರ"}],"qs":[{"q":"Which is NOT a function of management?","o":["Planning","Organising","Controlling","Manufacturing"],"a":3,"e":"Manufacturing is an operation, not a management function.","id":"bba1_1"},{"q":"Maslow's hierarchy is about","o":["human needs","prices","production","accounts"],"a":0,"e":"Needs: basic → safety → social → esteem → self-actualisation.","id":"bba1_2"},{"q":"SWOT: S, W, O and …","o":["Threats","Targets","Tasks","Trends"],"a":0,"e":"Threats.","id":"bba1_3"},{"q":"Top level of management","o":["Board / CEO","Supervisor","Clerk","Worker"],"a":0,"e":"Board and CEO set direction.","id":"bba1_4"},{"q":"Delegation means","o":["giving authority to a junior","firing staff","hiring","budgeting"],"a":0,"e":"Passing authority down.","id":"bba1_5"},{"q":"Which is NOT one of the 4 Ps?","o":["Product","Price","Place","People"],"a":3,"e":"4 Ps: Product, Price, Place, Promotion.","id":"bba1_6"},{"q":"Same tea pack: ₹10 in villages, ₹12 in cities. Pricing type?","o":["Penetration","Geographic","Skimming","Cost-plus"],"a":1,"e":"Price differs by place.","tag":"Workplace situation","id":"bba1_7"},{"q":"The HR department mainly handles","o":["people: hiring, training, pay","machines","taxes","stock"],"a":0,"e":"Human resources = people.","id":"bba1_8"}]},{"n":2,"name":"Finance & Excel","tag":"Workplace situation","cards":[{"t":"Break-even","b":"The point where sales just cover costs: no profit, no loss.","box":"Sales = Total cost","kn":"ಲಾಭವೂ ಇಲ್ಲ ನಷ್ಟವೂ ಇಲ್ಲ."},{"t":"Working capital","b":"Money to run daily work.","box":"Current assets − current liabilities","kn":"ದಿನನಿತ್ಯದ ಕೆಲಸಕ್ಕೆ ಹಣ."},{"t":"Excel basics","b":"Formulas start with =.","box":"=SUM(A1:A10) · =AVERAGE() · =MAX()","kn":"ಸೂತ್ರ = ಇಂದ ಶುರು."}],"qs":[{"q":"Excel: add A1 to A10","o":["=SUM(A1:A10)","=ADD(A1-A10)","SUM A1:A10","=TOTAL(A1,A10)"],"a":0,"e":"=SUM(range).","id":"bba2_1"},{"q":"Break-even point means","o":["no profit, no loss","highest profit","highest loss","closing day"],"a":0,"e":"Sales = costs.","id":"bba2_2"},{"q":"Working capital =","o":["Current assets − current liabilities","Total assets","Profit − tax","Sales − cost"],"a":0,"e":"Short-term money.","id":"bba2_3"},{"q":"=AVERAGE(10,20,30)","o":["20","60","30","10"],"a":0,"e":"60 ÷ 3 = 20.","id":"bba2_4"},{"q":"ROI stands for","o":["Return on Investment","Rate of Interest","Risk of Income","Return of Income"],"a":0,"e":"Return on Investment.","id":"bba2_5"},{"q":"Simple interest on ₹10,000 at 10% for 2 years","o":["₹1,000","₹2,000","₹2,100","₹200"],"a":1,"e":"10,000 × 10% × 2 = 2,000.","id":"bba2_6"},{"q":"A budget is","o":["a plan of income and spending","a bank","a tax","a bill"],"a":0,"e":"A money plan.","id":"bba2_7"},{"q":"=MAX(4, 9, 2)","o":["9","4","2","15"],"a":0,"e":"Largest value.","id":"bba2_8"}]}]},{"id":"bcom","g":"tech","course":"BCOM","name":"BCom Technical","emoji":"🧾","levels":[{"n":1,"name":"Accounting basics","tag":"Interview Q","cards":[{"t":"Golden rules","b":"Personal: debit the receiver, credit the giver. Real: debit what comes in, credit what goes out. Nominal: debit expenses and losses, credit incomes and gains.","box":"Personal · Real · Nominal","kn":"ಮೂರು ಸುವರ್ಣ ನಿಯಮಗಳು"},{"t":"Accounting equation","b":"Every entry keeps this balanced.","box":"Assets = Liabilities + Capital","kn":"ಆಸ್ತಿ = ಹೊಣೆ + ಬಂಡವಾಳ"},{"t":"Trial balance","b":"Checks that debits = credits in the ledger.","box":"Σ Debit = Σ Credit","kn":"ಡೆಬಿಟ್ = ಕ್ರೆಡಿಟ್"}],"qs":[{"q":"Golden rule for a personal account","o":["Debit the receiver, credit the giver","Debit what comes in","Debit all expenses","Credit everything"],"a":0,"e":"Personal accounts: receiver / giver.","id":"bcom1_1"},{"q":"Golden rule for a real account","o":["Debit what comes in, credit what goes out","Debit the receiver","Debit all incomes","Credit all assets"],"a":0,"e":"Real accounts: comes in / goes out.","id":"bcom1_2"},{"q":"Golden rule for a nominal account","o":["Debit expenses and losses, credit incomes and gains","Debit the giver","Debit what goes out","Credit expenses"],"a":0,"e":"Nominal: expenses / incomes.","id":"bcom1_3"},{"q":"Accounting equation","o":["Assets = Liabilities + Capital","Assets = Capital − Liabilities","Capital = Assets + Liabilities","Profit = Assets"],"a":0,"e":"A = L + C.","id":"bcom1_4"},{"q":"Rent paid in cash ₹5,000. Which account is debited?","o":["Rent A/c","Cash A/c","Capital A/c","Bank A/c"],"a":0,"e":"Expense → debit rent.","tag":"Workplace situation","id":"bcom1_5"},{"q":"Goods bought on credit from Ravi. Which account is credited?","o":["Ravi A/c","Purchases A/c","Cash A/c","Sales A/c"],"a":0,"e":"Ravi is the giver.","id":"bcom1_6"},{"q":"A trial balance checks","o":["arithmetic accuracy of the ledger","profit","tax","cash in hand"],"a":0,"e":"Debits = credits.","id":"bcom1_7"},{"q":"Depreciation is","o":["the fall in value of a fixed asset","a profit","a tax","a discount"],"a":0,"e":"Wear and tear over time.","id":"bcom1_8"}]},{"n":2,"name":"GST & Tally","tag":"Workplace situation","cards":[{"t":"Inside one state","b":"Sale inside Karnataka → CGST + SGST, half each.","box":"18% → CGST 9% + SGST 9%","kn":"ರಾಜ್ಯದೊಳಗೆ CGST + SGST"},{"t":"Between states","b":"Sale Karnataka → Maharashtra → IGST.","box":"18% → IGST 18%","kn":"ರಾಜ್ಯಗಳ ನಡುವೆ IGST"},{"t":"Tally vouchers","b":"Sales, Purchase, Payment, Receipt, Contra (cash ↔ bank), Journal.","box":"Contra = cash ↔ bank","kn":"ಕಾಂಟ್ರಾ = ನಗದು ↔ ಬ್ಯಾಂಕ್"}],"qs":[{"q":"₹10,000 sold inside Karnataka at 18% GST. Tax on the bill?","o":["IGST ₹1,800","CGST + SGST ₹1,800 (₹900 each)","CGST ₹1,800","No GST"],"a":1,"e":"Inside one state → CGST + SGST.","id":"bcom2_1"},{"q":"Sale from Karnataka to Maharashtra","o":["IGST","CGST + SGST","SGST only","No GST"],"a":0,"e":"Between states → IGST.","id":"bcom2_2"},{"q":"A GSTIN has how many characters?","o":["15","10","12","16"],"a":0,"e":"15 characters.","id":"bcom2_3"},{"q":"Input tax credit means","o":["GST paid on purchases is set off against GST on sales","a refund of income tax","a bank loan","a fine"],"a":0,"e":"You pay only the difference.","id":"bcom2_4"},{"q":"Tally: voucher for a cash sale","o":["Sales voucher","Payment voucher","Journal","Contra"],"a":0,"e":"Sales voucher.","id":"bcom2_5"},{"q":"A contra voucher is used for","o":["cash ↔ bank transfers","sales","purchases","salary"],"a":0,"e":"Cash deposited / withdrawn.","id":"bcom2_6"},{"q":"₹2,000 + 5% GST = ?","o":["₹2,100","₹2,050","₹2,005","₹2,500"],"a":0,"e":"2,000 × 1.05 = 2,100.","id":"bcom2_7"},{"q":"GST started in India in","o":["2017","2014","2019","2010"],"a":0,"e":"1 July 2017.","id":"bcom2_8"}]}]},{"id":"japanese","g":"jp","name":"Japanese","emoji":"🇯🇵","levels":[{"n":1,"name":"Hiragana: vowels","tag":"JLPT N5","cards":[{"t":"Japanese is sounds","b":"Like Kannada, each letter is one sound.","box":"あ い う え お = a i u e o","kn":"ಅ ಇ ಉ ಎ ಒ = あ い う え お"},{"t":"Write and say","b":"Say each one aloud 3 times.","box":"あ (a) · い (i) · う (u)","kn":"ಅ · ಇ · ಉ"},{"t":"Two more","b":"え sounds like 'e' in 'egg'; お like 'o' in 'oh'.","box":"え (e) · お (o)","kn":"ಎ · ಒ"}],"qs":[{"q":"あ is read as","o":["a","i","u","e"],"a":0,"e":"あ = a = ಅ.","id":"japanese1_1"},{"q":"い is read as","o":["i","a","o","u"],"a":0,"e":"い = i = ಇ.","id":"japanese1_2"},{"q":"う is read as","o":["u","e","o","a"],"a":0,"e":"う = u = ಉ.","id":"japanese1_3"},{"q":"え is read as","o":["e","a","i","o"],"a":0,"e":"え = e = ಎ.","id":"japanese1_4"},{"q":"お is read as","o":["o","u","a","e"],"a":0,"e":"お = o = ಒ.","id":"japanese1_5"},{"q":"Which hiragana is ಇ (i)?","o":["い","あ","う","お"],"a":0,"e":"い.","id":"japanese1_6"},{"q":"Which hiragana is ಒ (o)?","o":["お","え","あ","う"],"a":0,"e":"お.","id":"japanese1_7"},{"q":"あい is read as","o":["ai","ia","au","ui"],"a":0,"e":"あ + い = ai (means 'love').","id":"japanese1_8"}]},{"n":2,"name":"Hiragana: K row + first words","tag":"JLPT N5","cards":[{"t":"K row","b":"Add a 'k' sound: ka ki ku ke ko.","box":"か き く け こ","kn":"ಕ ಕಿ ಕು ಕೆ ಕೊ"},{"t":"First words","b":"Join letters to make words.","box":"あか (aka) = red · いく (iku) = go","kn":"ಅಕ = ಕೆಂಪು · ಇಕು = ಹೋಗು"},{"t":"Polite start","b":"Say this when you meet someone.","box":"はじめまして (hajimemashite) = nice to meet you","kn":"ನಿಮ್ಮನ್ನು ಭೇಟಿಯಾಗಿ ಸಂತೋಷ"}],"qs":[{"q":"か is read as","o":["ka","ki","ko","ku"],"a":0,"e":"か = ka = ಕ.","id":"japanese2_1"},{"q":"き is read as","o":["ki","ka","ke","ku"],"a":0,"e":"き = ki = ಕಿ.","id":"japanese2_2"},{"q":"こ is read as","o":["ko","ka","ku","ke"],"a":0,"e":"こ = ko = ಕೊ.","id":"japanese2_3"},{"q":"け is read as","o":["ke","ki","ka","ko"],"a":0,"e":"け = ke = ಕೆ.","id":"japanese2_4"},{"q":"く is read as","o":["ku","ko","ka","ki"],"a":0,"e":"く = ku = ಕು.","id":"japanese2_5"},{"q":"Which hiragana is ಕಿ (ki)?","o":["き","か","く","こ"],"a":0,"e":"き.","id":"japanese2_6"},{"q":"あか means","o":["red","blue","water","work"],"a":0,"e":"aka = red.","id":"japanese2_7"},{"q":"いく means","o":["to go","to eat","to see","to sleep"],"a":0,"e":"iku = to go.","id":"japanese2_8"}]}]}],"words":[{"w":"Punctual","m":"always on time","kn":"ಸಮಯಪಾಲಕ","ex":"Be punctual for your interview."},{"w":"Deadline","m":"the last time to finish","kn":"ಕೊನೆಯ ಗಡುವು","ex":"The deadline is Friday 5 pm."},{"w":"Negotiate","m":"talk to reach an agreement","kn":"ಮಾತುಕತೆ ನಡೆಸು","ex":"We negotiated the salary."},{"w":"Reliable","m":"can be trusted","kn":"ನಂಬಲರ್ಹ","ex":"She is a reliable team member."},{"w":"Colleague","m":"a person you work with","kn":"ಸಹೋದ್ಯೋಗಿ","ex":"My colleague helped me."},{"w":"Initiative","m":"starting something yourself","kn":"ಮುಂದಾಳತ್ವ","ex":"He took the initiative to fix it."},{"w":"Feedback","m":"comments to help you improve","kn":"ಪ್ರತಿಕ್ರಿಯೆ","ex":"Thank you for your feedback."},{"w":"Confident","m":"sure of yourself","kn":"ಆತ್ಮವಿಶ್ವಾಸದ","ex":"Speak in a confident voice."},{"w":"Opportunity","m":"a good chance","kn":"ಅವಕಾಶ","ex":"Thank you for this opportunity."},{"w":"Achieve","m":"reach a goal","kn":"ಸಾಧಿಸು","ex":"I achieved 90% in my exam."},{"w":"Efficient","m":"does work well without waste","kn":"ದಕ್ಷ","ex":"An efficient worker saves time."},{"w":"Flexible","m":"can change easily","kn":"ಹೊಂದಿಕೊಳ್ಳುವ","ex":"I am flexible with shift timings."},{"w":"Responsible","m":"in charge; can be trusted","kn":"ಜವಾಬ್ದಾರಿಯುತ","ex":"I was responsible for the college fest."},{"w":"Schedule","m":"a plan of times","kn":"ವೇಳಾಪಟ್ಟಿ","ex":"Let us schedule the meeting."},{"w":"Teamwork","m":"working together","kn":"ತಂಡದ ಕೆಲಸ","ex":"Teamwork makes the job easy."},{"w":"Leadership","m":"leading people","kn":"ನಾಯಕತ್ವ","ex":"She showed leadership in the NSS camp."},{"w":"Client","m":"a customer of a company","kn":"ಗ್ರಾಹಕ","ex":"The client liked our report."},{"w":"Improve","m":"make better","kn":"ಸುಧಾರಿಸು","ex":"I want to improve my English."},{"w":"Accurate","m":"exactly correct","kn":"ನಿಖರ","ex":"Accounts must be accurate."},{"w":"Communicate","m":"share ideas clearly","kn":"ಸಂವಹನ ಮಾಡು","ex":"Communicate clearly with your team."},{"w":"Motivated","m":"eager to work","kn":"ಉತ್ಸಾಹಿ","ex":"I am motivated to learn."},{"w":"Resume","m":"a 1-page list of your education and skills","kn":"ಸ್ವವಿವರ ಪತ್ರ","ex":"Keep your resume to one page."},{"w":"Interview","m":"a meeting to select you for a job","kn":"ಸಂದರ್ಶನ","ex":"My interview is at 10 am."},{"w":"Salary","m":"monthly pay","kn":"ಸಂಬಳ","ex":"The salary is credited on the 1st."},{"w":"Promotion","m":"moving to a higher post","kn":"ಬಡ್ತಿ","ex":"She got a promotion."},{"w":"Polite","m":"kind and respectful in words","kn":"ವಿನಯಶೀಲ","ex":"Be polite on the phone."},{"w":"Prepare","m":"get ready","kn":"ತಯಾರಾಗು","ex":"Prepare well for the test."},{"w":"Patience","m":"calm waiting","kn":"ತಾಳ್ಮೆ","ex":"Learning a language needs patience."},{"w":"Goal","m":"what you want to reach","kn":"ಗುರಿ","ex":"My goal is an IT job."},{"w":"Consistent","m":"the same every day","kn":"ಸ್ಥಿರ","ex":"Be consistent with your practice."}],"tips":[{"c":"Resume","t":"One page. Projects first, hobbies last.","b":"Name, phone, email, LinkedIn on top. Your best project in 2 lines: what you built + tool used. No photo, no father's name, no full address.","kn":"ಒಂದೇ ಪುಟ. ಮೊದಲು ಪ್ರಾಜೆಕ್ಟ್, ಕೊನೆಗೆ ಹವ್ಯಾಸ."},{"c":"Resume","t":"Use action words","b":"Start each line with a verb: Built, Led, Organised, Improved. Add a number where you can: 'Organised a fest for 400 students'.","kn":"ಪ್ರತಿ ಸಾಲು ಕ್ರಿಯಾಪದದಿಂದ ಶುರು ಮಾಡಿ."},{"c":"HR round","t":"'Tell me about yourself' in 60 seconds","b":"Name → course → 1 project → 1 strength → why this company. Practise it aloud on the 🎤 English page.","kn":"ಹೆಸರು → ಕೋರ್ಸ್ → ಪ್ರಾಜೆಕ್ಟ್ → ಶಕ್ತಿ → ಏಕೆ ಈ ಕಂಪನಿ."},{"c":"HR round","t":"Research the company","b":"Know what the company does, one product, and where its office is. Saying it shows you are serious.","kn":"ಕಂಪನಿಯ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಮೊದಲೇ ತಿಳಿದುಕೊಳ್ಳಿ."},{"c":"Online test","t":"Never leave a question blank","b":"Most company tests have no negative marks. Skip a hard one after 60 seconds, come back at the end, and guess if time runs out.","kn":"ಖಾಲಿ ಬಿಡಬೇಡಿ; 60 ಸೆಕೆಂಡ್ ನಂತರ ಮುಂದೆ ಹೋಗಿ."},{"c":"Online test","t":"Check your setup the day before","b":"Charged phone / laptop, stable internet, ID card ready, quiet room. Log in 15 minutes early.","kn":"ಹಿಂದಿನ ದಿನವೇ ಇಂಟರ್ನೆಟ್, ಚಾರ್ಜ್ ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿಸಿ."},{"c":"GD","t":"Speak early, not loud","b":"Be among the first 3 to speak. Add one point with an example, then let others talk. Sum up at the end if nobody does.","kn":"ಮೊದಲ 3 ಜನರಲ್ಲಿ ಮಾತನಾಡಿ."},{"c":"GD","t":"Agree, then add","b":"'I agree with Ravi, and I would add that…' sounds team-friendly and still shows your idea.","kn":"ಒಪ್ಪಿ, ನಂತರ ನಿಮ್ಮ ಅಂಶ ಸೇರಿಸಿ."},{"c":"Dress","t":"Plain formal, ironed, clean shoes","b":"Light shirt, dark trousers, formal shoes. Girls: formal kurta or shirt. No bright colours or big logos.","kn":"ಸರಳ ಫಾರ್ಮಲ್ ಉಡುಪು, ಇಸ್ತ್ರಿ ಮಾಡಿದ ಬಟ್ಟೆ."},{"c":"LinkedIn","t":"Add your Davan certificate","b":"Clear photo, headline like 'BCA 2027 · Java · SQL', and your 🏅 Davan Placement certificates under Licences & certifications.","kn":"Davan ಪ್ರಮಾಣಪತ್ರವನ್ನು LinkedIn ಗೆ ಸೇರಿಸಿ."},{"c":"Interview day","t":"Carry 3 printed resumes","b":"Plus your ID, a pen, and certificates in a file. Reach 30 minutes early.","kn":"3 ರೆಸ್ಯೂಮ್ ಪ್ರತಿ ತೆಗೆದುಕೊಂಡು ಹೋಗಿ."},{"c":"Interview day","t":"Ask one question at the end","b":"'What does a fresher learn in the first 6 months here?' shows interest. Never ask only about salary first.","kn":"ಕೊನೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಒಂದು ಪ್ರಶ್ನೆ ಕೇಳಿ."}],"jp":[{"j":"しごと","r":"shigoto","ks":"ಶಿಗೊತೊ","kn":"ಕೆಲಸ","en":"work"},{"j":"ありがとう","r":"arigatou","ks":"ಅರಿಗಾತೊ","kn":"ಧನ್ಯವಾದ","en":"thank you"},{"j":"みず","r":"mizu","ks":"ಮಿಜು","kn":"ನೀರು","en":"water"},{"j":"がっこう","r":"gakkou","ks":"ಗಕ್ಕೊ","kn":"ಶಾಲೆ","en":"school"},{"j":"ともだち","r":"tomodachi","ks":"ತೊಮೊದಚಿ","kn":"ಸ್ನೇಹಿತ","en":"friend"},{"j":"せんせい","r":"sensei","ks":"ಸೆನ್ಸೇ","kn":"ಶಿಕ್ಷಕ","en":"teacher"},{"j":"たべる","r":"taberu","ks":"ತಬೆರು","kn":"ತಿನ್ನು","en":"to eat"},{"j":"のむ","r":"nomu","ks":"ನೊಮು","kn":"ಕುಡಿ","en":"to drink"},{"j":"いく","r":"iku","ks":"ಇಕು","kn":"ಹೋಗು","en":"to go"},{"j":"くる","r":"kuru","ks":"ಕುರು","kn":"ಬಾ","en":"to come"},{"j":"おはよう","r":"ohayou","ks":"ಒಹಾಯೊ","kn":"ಶುಭೋದಯ","en":"good morning"},{"j":"こんにちは","r":"konnichiwa","ks":"ಕೊನ್ನಿಚಿವಾ","kn":"ನಮಸ್ಕಾರ","en":"hello"},{"j":"すみません","r":"sumimasen","ks":"ಸುಮಿಮಸೆನ್","kn":"ಕ್ಷಮಿಸಿ","en":"excuse me / sorry"},{"j":"なまえ","r":"namae","ks":"ನಮಎ","kn":"ಹೆಸರು","en":"name"},{"j":"かいしゃ","r":"kaisha","ks":"ಕಾಯಿಶಾ","kn":"ಕಂಪನಿ","en":"company"}],"speak":[{"s":"Could you please tell me more about the job role?","kn":"ದಯವಿಟ್ಟು ಈ ಕೆಲಸದ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ಹೇಳುತ್ತೀರಾ?"},{"s":"Thank you for giving me this opportunity.","kn":"ಈ ಅವಕಾಶ ಕೊಟ್ಟಿದ್ದಕ್ಕೆ ಧನ್ಯವಾದ."},{"s":"I am a final-year student and I am a quick learner.","kn":"ನಾನು ಅಂತಿಮ ವರ್ಷದ ವಿದ್ಯಾರ್ಥಿ, ಬೇಗ ಕಲಿಯುತ್ತೇನೆ."},{"s":"I worked on a project to manage college attendance.","kn":"ಕಾಲೇಜು ಹಾಜರಾತಿ ಪ್ರಾಜೆಕ್ಟ್ ಮಾಡಿದ್ದೇನೆ."},{"s":"My strength is that I never give up.","kn":"ನನ್ನ ಶಕ್ತಿ: ನಾನು ಸೋಲು ಒಪ್ಪಿಕೊಳ್ಳುವುದಿಲ್ಲ."},{"s":"I am comfortable working in a team.","kn":"ತಂಡದಲ್ಲಿ ಕೆಲಸ ಮಾಡಲು ನನಗೆ ಇಷ್ಟ."},{"s":"Sorry, could you repeat the question, please?","kn":"ಕ್ಷಮಿಸಿ, ಪ್ರಶ್ನೆಯನ್ನು ಮತ್ತೊಮ್ಮೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತೀರಾ?"},{"s":"I will send the report by five pm today.","kn":"ಇಂದು ಸಂಜೆ ಐದರೊಳಗೆ ವರದಿ ಕಳುಹಿಸುತ್ತೇನೆ."},{"s":"I look forward to hearing from you.","kn":"ನಿಮ್ಮ ಉತ್ತರಕ್ಕಾಗಿ ಕಾಯುತ್ತೇನೆ."},{"s":"I am willing to relocate for this job.","kn":"ಈ ಕೆಲಸಕ್ಕಾಗಿ ಬೇರೆ ಊರಿಗೆ ಹೋಗಲು ಸಿದ್ಧ."}]}